1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,679
Make a list of the habits that you want to have in your life.
列一张清单，写出你想在生活中养成的习惯。

2
00:00:02,679 --> 00:00:06,840
If you want to drink more water because you don't drink enough or if you want to start meditating.
如果你喝水不够，想多喝水，或想开始冥想……

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:10,079
Maybe if you want to start journaling right regularly write them all down.
也许你想开始经常写日记，把它们都记下来。

4
00:00:10,079 --> 00:00:16,440
Make sure again that you aren't overburdening yourself with so many things that it's just not even possible for you to do them all in one day.
再次注意，别给自己加太多事，导致一天根本做不完。

5
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:19,000
And find ways to add them into your routine.
然后找到把这些习惯加入日常流程的方法。

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,079
One of the most effective techniques for building healthy habits is habit stacking.
她认为，培养好习惯的有效方法之一是习惯叠加。

7
00:00:23,079 --> 00:00:25,949
I learned about this in the book atomic habits by james clear.
我从 James Clear 的《原子习惯》里学到这个概念。

8
00:00:25,959 --> 00:00:30,959
But it talks about how when you kind of master one habit or when you already have one habit that you do.
书里说，当你掌握了一种习惯，或本来就有一个固定习惯时……

9
00:00:30,959 --> 00:00:34,320
Like you take a shower every night maybe you want to start reading at night.
比如你每晚洗澡，而你又想开始晚上阅读。

10
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:36,789
You could take a shower and then read for a little bit.
那就洗完澡后读一小会儿。

11
00:00:36,799 --> 00:00:39,560
Like you tack a habit on to one that you're already doing.
这就像把一个习惯接到你已有的习惯上。

12
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:45,639
So something that I actually started doing was I wanted to read every day but I couldn't figure out what a good time of day for me to read was.
我自己想每天阅读，但一直没找到合适的阅读时段。

13
00:00:45,639 --> 00:00:50,679
But I thought okay well in the mornings you know I do my morning routine and then I make breakfast and then I start on work.
后来我想，早晨我完成晨间流程、做早餐，再开始工作。

14
00:00:50,679 --> 00:00:53,040
Why don't I just read while I eat breakfast.
为什么不一边吃早餐一边阅读呢？

15
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:55,799
Like I add a habit onto a habit that I'm already doing.
这样我就把一个新习惯加到了已有习惯上。

16
00:00:55,799 --> 00:00:59,359
The other thing that goes along with this is make habits easy for yourself.
与此相关的另一点，是让习惯容易执行。

17
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:03,639
If you want to read every day for example get a book and like put it on your pillow.
例如想每天读书，就把书放在枕头上。

18
00:01:03,639 --> 00:01:06,239
So that you go to go to bed and you're like my book is right there.
这样去睡觉时，你会发现书就在眼前。

19
00:01:06,239 --> 00:01:10,480
You don't have to go out of your way to go find a book or like hunt it down it's right there.
不用特地到处找书，它就在那里。

20
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:16,000
I keep my book on the kitchen table so every time I sit down to eat breakfast it's right there I'm reminded of my habit.
我把书放在厨房桌上，每次坐下吃早餐就会被提醒这个习惯。

21
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,960
That I want to have of reading every day.
提醒我自己想养成每天阅读的习惯。

22
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:25,159
If eating healthier is like a habit that you want to have make eating healthier easier for yourself by buying healthy groceries.
如果想养成更健康饮食的习惯，可以买好食材，让这件事容易些。

23
00:01:25,159 --> 00:01:30,320
And then prepping them for yourself so that it's really easy to grab like fresh cut up fruits and vegetables out of the fridge.
再提前处理好，这样就能轻松从冰箱取出切好的果蔬。

24
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:36,839
And this goes for again if you're trying to build a routine of healthy habits and maybe it's too overwhelming to start doing all of them at once.
如果你要建立习惯流程，但同时开始所有习惯让你应付不过来……

25
00:01:36,839 --> 00:01:41,560
Start doing one of them and then after you kind of master that one habit you can tack another one onto it.
就先做其中一个，掌握后再叠加另一个。

26
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:45,640
And after a while they're like second nature they're not something you even really have to think about doing.
过一阵它们就像第二天性，不用刻意思考就会去做。

27
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:52,400
Minimize distractions figure out what your distractions are for me and probably for a lot of people it's my phone often times.
减少分心，先找出分心源。对我和很多人来说，经常就是手机。

28
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:57,719
So if I want to be really productive but I'm finding myself tempted to pick up my phone and start scrolling or whatever.
我想高效做事，却忍不住拿手机刷内容时……

29
00:01:57,719 --> 00:02:02,640
I will literally put my phone in the other room so that doing the distraction becomes difficult for me.
我真的会把手机放在另一个房间，让分心变得不容易。

30
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:06,240
Like make the distraction difficult again this is something from atomic habits.
让分心更麻烦，这也来自《原子习惯》。

31
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:12,159
But like make the bad habit that you don't want to do or whatever the distraction is so difficult that you're not even going to go out of your way to do it.
让坏习惯或分心的事足够麻烦，你就不愿特地去做。

32
00:02:12,159 --> 00:02:15,520
Another thing that I like to do is put time limits on my social media apps.
我还会给社交媒体应用设置时间限制。

33
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:19,719
And then when the timer pops up I'm like okay that's that's it that's all I have on there for today.
提醒弹出时，我就想，好了，今天只用到这里。

34
00:02:19,719 --> 00:02:24,279
Overall in this period another really big thing is to kind of go ghost mode.
这段时间另一件事，是进入她所说的低调专注模式。

35
00:02:24,279 --> 00:02:28,440
The idea is that you're not putting time into people who aren't giving you back the time of day.
意思是，不再把时间花在那些不愿回应你的人身上。

36
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:34,520
You're kind of working on yourself and you're not sitting for hours on your phone like living vicariously through the lives of others.
专注自己，而不是花几小时看手机，通过别人的生活获得间接体验。

37
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:38,440
You're living in your own real life with the real people who are around you.
要过你真实的生活，与身边真实的人相处。

38
00:02:38,440 --> 00:02:43,159
It's not to say like don't text your friends or whatever but just if you have like somebody who's been playing with your feelings.
不是说别给朋友发消息，而是如果某人一直玩弄你的感情……

39
00:02:43,159 --> 00:02:46,480
And you're like you know what I don't need this in my life I'm done talking to you.
你可能会想，我不需要这种关系，我不想再聊了。

40
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:49,960
Cut some people off if you have to if they're not good for you if they're toxic for you.
必要时与不适合自己、对自己有伤害的人断开联系，这是她的看法。

41
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:54,599
If there's a certain app on your phone that's just such a time suck and it doesn't make you feel good about yourself.
如果某个应用消耗大量时间，还让你对自己感觉很差……

42
00:02:54,599 --> 00:02:57,240
And you're like I don't even want to have this app delete it.
你觉得根本不想用它，那就删除它。

43
00:02:57,240 --> 00:03:02,560
Because at the end of the day these distractions will inhibit your growth and they will keep you from reaching your full potential.
因为在她看来，这些分心会阻碍成长，让你无法发挥全部潜力。

44
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:08,719
Work on your physical fitness take this time to work out move your body it's good for you in so many ways.
她接着建议关注身体状态，抽时间活动身体，并认为有很多好处。

45
00:03:08,719 --> 00:03:11,080
I mean your body needs to move it wants to move.
她说身体需要活动，也想活动。

46
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:15,480
Even though it's colder and it's kind of harder to get outside sometimes I don't even feel like going on a walk.
即使天冷、不容易出门，有时我也不想散步。

47
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:21,160
But even that is such a simple way to get some steps in like get your steps up feel good move your body get outside.
但散步是增加步数的简单方式；她鼓励活动一下、走到户外。
